<header><p class="st-kicker">emirate · Iberia</p><h1 class="st-title">Taifa of Toledo</h1><p class="st-meta">1010 CE – 1085 CE (approx.) · capital Toledo</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">The central taifa of al-Andalus under the Dhul-Nunid dynasty, famous for its scientists and for its fall to Alfonso VI of Castile in 1085.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/toledo">Toledo</a>, the old Visigothic capital and frontier city of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/middle-march-al-andalus">Middle March</a>, threw off caliphal rule around 1010. Its notables first chose local leaders, then invited the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/berbers">Berber</a> <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/dhul-nunid-dynasty">Banu Dhi al-Nun</a>, lords of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ucles">Uclés</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/huete">Huete</a>, whose <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ismail-al-zafir">Ismail al-Zafir</a> established the dynasty in the 1030s.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p>Al-Mamun (1043-1075) made <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/toledo">Toledo</a> one of the most powerful <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/taifa">taifas</a>, conquering <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/valencia">Valencia</a> in 1065 and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cordoba">Córdoba</a> in 1075. His court sponsored science: the astronomer al-Zarqali produced the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/toledan-tables">Toledan Tables</a>, and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ibn-wafid">Ibn Wafid</a> laid out botanical gardens. A large <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mozarabs">Mozarab</a> Christian and Jewish population lived in the city, and tribute was paid to León and <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/kingdom-of-castile">Castile</a>.</p><h2>Decline and legacy</h2><p>Al-Mamun's grandson <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/yahya-al-qadir">al-Qadir</a>, unpopular and dependent on <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/kingdom-of-castile">Castile</a>, surrendered <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/toledo">Toledo</a> to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/alfonso-vi-of-castile">Alfonso VI</a> on 25 May 1085. The loss shocked <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/al-andalus">al-Andalus</a> and led the remaining <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/taifa">taifas</a> to call in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/almoravid-empire">Almoravids</a>. Toledo became a centre of translation from Arabic into <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/latin">Latin</a>.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><figure class="st-fig"><img src="/images/states/taifa-of-toledo.jpg" alt="Taifa of Toledo" width="320" height="271"><figcaption>Image: Tyk · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Location_map_Taifa_of_Toledo.svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">source</a></figcaption></figure><dl class="st-facts"><dt>Years</dt><dd>1010 CE – 1085 CE (approx.)</dd><dt>Century</dt><dd><a href="/centuries/11th-century">11th century</a></dd><dt>Type</dt><dd>emirate</dd><dt>Character</dt><dd>feudal</dd><dt>Capital</dt><dd>Toledo</dd><dt>Rulers</dt><dd>Ismail al-Zafir, al-Mamun, Yahya al-Qadir</dd><dt>Religion</dt><dd>Sunni Islam</dd><dt>Language</dt><dd>Andalusi Arabic, Mozarabic</dd><dt>Today</dt><dd><a href="/countries/spain">Spain</a></dd><dt>Also</dt><dd>Dhul-Nunid Kingdom of Toledo</dd></dl><figure class="st-locator"><a href="/atlas?year=1048&amp;focus=taifa-of-toledo" aria-label="Taifa of Toledo on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="4581 751 640 512" role="img" aria-label="Map: where Taifa of Toledo lay"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-tie" d="M4901 1007L4881 1071M4901 1007L4910 928M4901 1007L4991 1020"/><path class="map-dot-n" d="M4881 1071h0M4910 928h0M4991 1020h0"/><path class="map-dot-halo" d="M4901 1007h0"/><path class="map-dot-me" d="M4901 1007h0"/></svg></a><figcaption>The dot marks Toledo. <a href="/atlas?year=1048&amp;focus=taifa-of-toledo">On the atlas &rarr;</a></figcaption></figure></aside></div>
